WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.860
A bare hillside.

2
00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.300
Withered reeds.

3
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.680
No birds.

4
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:10.410
A voice asks: "O what can ail thee,
knight-at-arms," The knight is alone,

5
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.110
pale and sick.

6
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.790
How did he end up here?

7
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.290
In a meadow, he met a
lady, a faery's child.

8
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.870
She found him honey and sweet roots.

9
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.590
And she said: "I love thee true."

10
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.920
A love story.

11
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.060
So why is the knight left alone, dying?

12
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.810
In this mission, you'll
meet John Keats's ballad,

13
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.180
written in April 1819 in a
letter to his brother George.

14
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.530
You'll gather the signs
of the knight's sickness,

15
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.550
and the bleak land around him.

16
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.990
And you'll step inside his dream
of pale kings and warriors.

17
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.620
Your mission: explain why
the knight is left dying.
